# Git workflow

- Follow the repository's branch conventions; prefer focused branches.
- **PRs** — small, focused, green CI, description template, self-review first.
- **No force-push** to `main`/`develop`; no secrets in commits.
- **CHANGELOG** maintained if project ships versions.

## Commit messages (required)

Use **Conventional Commits**. Short subject, imperative mood, no trailing period.

### Format

```text
type(scope): summary

optional body
```

### Types

| Type | When |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Internal restructure, same behavior |
| `style` | Formatting / visual-only UI polish |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, config, housekeeping |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `ci` | CI/CD only |

### Scope

Optional but preferred when clear: `web`, `api`, `portal`, `auth`, `clinics`, `i18n`, …

### Examples

```text
feat(portal): add Super Admin clinics live search
fix(auth): block letters in phone input
style(portal): match Search and Add Clinic button widths
refactor(web): extract PortalClinicsPanel
chore: update Cursor git commit conventions
```

### Do not

- Long essay subjects or “Update/Fix stuff”
- Subject that only lists files
- Mixing unrelated changes in one commit (split instead)
